  "faqWhatAreHeadersTitle": "What are headers?",
  "faqWhatAreHeadersSubtitle": "Organize recipes into sections",
  "faqWhatAreHeadersAnswer": "Headers let you divide your recipe ingredients and steps into sections. For example, you could have separate sections for 'Sauce', 'Dough', and 'Topping' in a pizza recipe. They make long recipes much easier to follow.",
  "faqWhatAreSublinkedTitle": "What are sublinked recipes?",
  "faqWhatAreSublinkedSubtitle": "Connect related recipes together",
  "faqWhatAreSublinkedAnswer": "Sublinked recipes let you connect related recipes together. For example, a Margherita Pizza recipe can link to your Pizza Dough recipe. When viewing the main recipe, you can tap the linked recipe to jump straight to it — no searching needed.",
  "faqMacroCalcTitle": "How to use the Macro Calculator",
  "faqMacroCalcSubtitle": "Auto-calculate calories and macros for any recipe",
  "faqMacroCalcStep1Title": "Open a recipe",
  "faqMacroCalcStep1Desc": "Open any recipe to view its details.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep2Title": "Find the Nutrition section",
  "faqMacroCalcStep2Desc": "Scroll to the bottom of the recipe. If no nutrition data exists yet, you'll see an empty state — tap it to start the calculator.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep3Title": "View the calculator",
  "faqMacroCalcStep3Desc": "The calculator automatically matches your ingredients to the USDA food database and shows the match rate, calories, and macro breakdown.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep4Title": "Enter manually",
  "faqMacroCalcStep4Desc": "Tap 'Enter Manually' to edit nutrition values by hand if you prefer to input your own data instead of using the auto-calculated results.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep5Title": "Review ingredient matches",
  "faqMacroCalcStep5Desc": "Scroll down to see each ingredient matched to a USDA food item. Sublinked recipes (like Pizza Dough) use their own stored nutrition instead.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep5Tip": "Not sure what a sublinked recipe is? Check out the 'What are sublinked recipes?' section in the FAQ!",
  "faqMacroCalcStep6Title": "Browse the USDA database",
  "faqMacroCalcStep6Desc": "Tap any ingredient to search the USDA database for a better match. You can pick from thousands of verified food items.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep7Title": "Linked recipe nutrition",
  "faqMacroCalcStep7Desc": "Ingredients linked to other recipes show the linked recipe's nutrition data. You can adjust the scale to use a fraction of the linked recipe.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep8Title": "Save your results",
  "faqMacroCalcStep8Desc": "Tap Save to store the nutrition data. The macros will now appear on your recipe with charts and detailed breakdowns per serving.",
  "faqMacroCalcStep9Title": "Customize the display",
  "faqMacroCalcStep9Desc": "Go to Settings > Nutrition Display to choose which nutrients to show and how the charts are displayed.",
  "faqWhatIsMacroCalcTitle": "What is the Macro Calculator?",
  "faqWhatIsMacroCalcSubtitle": "Automatic nutrition estimation for recipes",
  "faqWhatIsMacroCalcAnswer": "The Macro Calculator automatically estimates the nutritional content of your recipes by matching each ingredient to the USDA food database. It calculates calories, protein, carbs, fat, fiber, sugar, sodium, and more — all per serving. You can find it in the Nutrition section of any recipe.",
  "faqImportFailedTitle": "Why did my import fail?",
  "faqImportFailedSubtitle": "Common reasons and fixes",
  "faqImportFailedAnswer": "Imports can fail for a few reasons:\n\n• The website may block automated access — try copying the recipe text and using Text Import instead.\n• The link may have expired or be private — make sure it’s a public link.\n• Some sites use formats that are harder to parse — try the AI import as an alternative.\n• Check your internet connection and try again.",
  "faqDeviceTransferTitle": "Can I import from other devices?",
  "faqDeviceTransferSubtitle": "Transfer recipes between phones and tablets",
  "faqDeviceTransferAnswer": "Yes! Use the Device Transfer feature in Settings > Data > Device Transfer. Generate a code on your old device and enter it on your new one. All your recipes, cookbooks, and images will be transferred.",
